# 41. Migration from Frontend State

During early frontend development, Teams and scores are stored in React state.

For example:

    const [teams, setTeams] = useState(...)

This is temporary development data.

Once the Spring Boot API is integrated:

    React State
         |
         | replaced by
         v
    REST API
         |
         v
    Spring Boot
         |
         v
    PostgreSQL

The frontend will request Team information from the backend rather than treating hard-coded React objects as permanent application data.

---

# 42. Migration from Firebase

The rebuilt application does not require the original Firebase data structure to determine the new relational schema.

If historical Firebase data needs to be preserved, a migration process can later:

    Firebase
       |
       v
    Export
       |
       v
    Transform
       |
       v
    Validate
       |
       v
    PostgreSQL

The transformation process would map:

    Firebase event
        -> Event / EventSettings

    Firebase teams
        -> Team

    Firebase members
        -> TeamMember

    Firebase scores
        -> Team / ScoreEvent

Historical score events can only be migrated if the original Firebase data contains sufficient history.

If only current scores were retained, historical ScoreEvent records cannot be reconstructed reliably and should not be invented.

